       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. That is more than double the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults, and 3,000 mg is about three times the usual single dose of 1,000 mg. At this level there is a serious risk of acute liver injury, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**\n- **3000 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do intend the original dose, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note documenting that. Otherwise, tell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away."
